{"name":"High Note","hex":"#867a88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high note","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The highest and usually climactic note of a song or composition, especially one that is difficult to reach.","A climax or best achievement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_note"}],"entries":[{"title":"High Note (film)","blocks":[{"text":"High Note is a 1960 American animated short film directed by Chuck Jones and written by Michael Maltese. It was originally released by Warner Bros. Pictures on December 3, 1960, as part of the Looney Tunes series. The short features no dialogue, relying solely on the animation and music to carry the plot. It was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Short Film (Cartoon) in 1961, losing to Gene Deitch's Munro."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Note_(film)","wikidata":"Q1610534"},{"title":"The High Note","blocks":[{"text":"The High Note is a 2020 American comedy drama film directed by Nisha Ganatra and written by Flora Greeson. It stars Dakota Johnson, Tracee Ellis Ross, Kelvin Harrison Jr., Zoë Chao, Bill Pullman, Eddie Izzard, and Ice Cube, and follows a famous singer's personal assistant who wants to become a music producer."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6d/The_High_Note_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_High_Note","wikidata":"Q64990050"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_rectangle.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_rectangle.jpg","share":0.569375},{"title":"Grey squirrel (Sciurus carolinensis) 02","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Grey_squirrel_%28Sciurus_carolinensis%29_02.jpg/500px-Grey_squirrel_%28Sciurus_carolinensis%29_02.jpg","rati